<task id="030" project="messaging-communication-app-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Event Grid webhook ingress (subscription-validation handshake) → Service Bus job</title>
    <phase>W3 — Inbound Capture Pipeline</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>6</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>012,021</dependencies>
    <blocks>031</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, communication, jobs</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Adds a NEW public webhook endpoint (Event Grid ingress) + Service Bus job enqueue to `Sprk.Bff.Api` — inbound-facing, security-relevant (unvalidated webhook must not enqueue), BFF-touching (`.cs`, endpoint + Services/Communication + Services/Jobs hot-path). Requires publish-size + CVE + code-review + adr-check per root §10.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W3</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-02</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Build the ACS Event Grid **webhook ingress** — the transport boundary that turns ACS chat events into a queued job for downstream normalize-and-persist (task 031):

    • **Event Grid webhook ingress endpoint** — a BFF endpoint that receives Event Grid deliveries for the ACS system topic. It MUST handle the Event Grid **subscription-validation handshake**: on a `Microsoft.EventGrid.SubscriptionValidationEvent`, echo back the `validationCode` (synchronous validation-response) so Event Grid activates the subscription; on real chat events (`Microsoft.Communication.ChatMessageReceivedInThread` and siblings), accept the batch and enqueue.
    • **Enqueue a Service Bus job** — for each validated chat event, enqueue a job onto the existing `Services/Jobs/` contract (reuse `JobSubmissionService` / the job envelope — do NOT invent a new queue or job pipeline). The endpoint's job is thin: validate the webhook, handle the handshake, enqueue, return fast. It MUST NOT persist `sprk_communication`, normalize the event, or run enrichment inline — that is task 031's Service Bus job handler.

    Only a **validated** webhook enqueues: reject/ignore deliveries that fail the Event Grid validation (subscription-validation handshake for activation; and, where ACS/Event Grid supports it, verify the delivery is genuinely from the subscribed system topic before enqueue). No unvalidated payload reaches the job queue.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF Communication architect. Authority on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` inbound capture + `Services/Jobs/`. Fluent in ADR-045 (channel seams — ingestor), ADR-046 (ACS transport — task 007), ADR-004/ADR-036 (job contract / background-job infra), ADR-008 (endpoint filters), ADR-019 (ProblemDetails), ADR-027 (per-customer ACS + Event Grid provisioning — task 012), and `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A BFF Event Grid ingress endpoint receives ACS system-topic deliveries, correctly answers the subscription-validation handshake (echo `validationCode`), and for each validated chat event enqueues a job onto the existing `Services/Jobs/` contract. The endpoint is thin — validate, handshake, enqueue, return; it does NOT normalize/persist/enrich. Unvalidated webhooks do not enqueue. Build clean; endpoint + handshake + enqueue tests pass; publish-size (vs ~45.30 MB) + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported; `/conflict-check` before PR.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      **Mirror the email inbound rails; reuse the job contract.** The email inbound path already flows Graph webhook → job → `IncomingCommunicationProcessor` over the `Services/Jobs/` contract (idempotency, DLQ, retry). Messaging's inbound is the ACS analog: `participant sends → ACS → Event Grid → webhook ingress (validated) → Service Bus job → normalizer → ingestor persists → enrichment` (design §4, §8.3). This task builds ONLY the first hop — the Event Grid webhook ingress and the job enqueue. Task 021 shipped the `ICommunicationChannelIngestor` seam + `MessagingIngestor`; task 031 builds the Service Bus job handler that normalizes the ACS event into a `NormalizedMessage` and calls the ingestor with idempotent dedupe + DLQ. Task 012 provisions the per-customer ACS resource + Event Grid system topic/subscription pointing at this endpoint (+ dead-letter Storage).

      **Event Grid delivery semantics (design §8.3):** subscription-validation handshake on activation (echo `validationCode`); events are **at-least-once, unordered, may duplicate** — so the endpoint is deliberately thin and idempotency lives in 031's handler (dedupe on ACS message id). The endpoint returns 200 fast to avoid Event Grid retries piling up; real processing is async on the queue.

      **§11 Component Justification.** The ingress endpoint is NEW public surface: (Existing) no ACS/Event Grid ingress exists — grep confirms no Event Grid webhook in the BFF; (Extension) the email Graph-webhook ingress is Graph-subscription-specific and cannot receive Event Grid schema/handshake — a distinct transport; (Cost-of-doing-nothing) without this endpoint, no inbound ACS message can enter the pipeline at all — Event Grid has nowhere to deliver, so chat is send-only.

      Scope discipline: webhook ingress + validation handshake + job enqueue ONLY. Do NOT normalize the event, persist `sprk_communication`, run enrichment, implement idempotency/dedupe, or wire the DLQ inline — all of that is 031's Service Bus job handler.
    </background>
