  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read the `Services/Jobs/` contract (`JobSubmissionService`, `JobContract`, `ServiceBusJobProcessor`, `IncomingCommunicationJobHandler`) to see how the email inbound job is enqueued + the envelope shape. Read the existing Graph webhook-validation precedent in `Infrastructure/Auth/`. Read task 012's Event Grid system-topic/subscription config + task 021's `ICommunicationChannelIngestor` (the eventual consumer).</step>
    <step order="2">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F/§G + `.claude/agent-memory/researcher/acs-chat-integration-2026-07-16.md` (Event Grid handshake + at-least-once/duplicate/unordered semantics + dead-letter). Grep-confirm no Event Grid ingress exists (§11 evidence).</step>
    <step order="3">Add the Event Grid ingress endpoint: on `Microsoft.EventGrid.SubscriptionValidationEvent`, return the synchronous validation response echoing `validationCode`; on ACS chat events (`ChatMessageReceivedInThread` + siblings), verify the delivery originates from the subscribed ACS system topic, then continue. Return fast; ProblemDetails on malformed input.</step>
    <step order="4">For each validated chat event, build a job envelope (carry the ACS event payload / message id + thread id needed by 031) and enqueue via `JobSubmissionService` onto the existing Service Bus contract. Define the new job kind/handler-name that 031 will implement — but do NOT implement the handler body here (031 owns normalize+persist+dedupe+DLQ).</step>
    <step order="5">Register the endpoint + any new service in `Program.cs` / `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010; ADR-032 Null-Object + unconditional registration if feature-gated).</step>
    <step order="6">Write tests: a `SubscriptionValidationEvent` yields the correct validation-code echo (subscription activates); a `ChatMessageReceivedInThread` event enqueues exactly one job with the expected envelope; an unvalidated/wrong-topic delivery does NOT enqueue; a malformed payload returns ProblemDetails and enqueues nothing. Prefer vertical-slice seam tests per ADR-038 (no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`).</step>
    <step order="7">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication`; confirm existing inbound/job tests still pass.</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o c:/tmp/msg-030-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline (any Event Grid/ACS SDK add is thin). ≥+5 MB justify; ≥55 MB architecture review; ≥60 MB HARD STOP.</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVE.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff (EXPLICIT focus on the webhook-validation / unvalidated-payload security boundary); `adr-check` against `spec.md` (ADR-004/036 reuse-the-job-contract, ADR-046 transport, ADR-008/019 endpoint hygiene). Resolve Critical findings (path C) or surface an ADR conflict (root §6.5).</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/` + `Services/Jobs/` BFF hot-path).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (030 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (endpoint route, validation approach, job kind/envelope contract 031 consumes).</step>
  </steps>

