  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The Event Grid ingress endpoint answers the subscription-validation handshake — a `Microsoft.EventGrid.SubscriptionValidationEvent` yields a response echoing the `validationCode` so the subscription activates.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A validated `ChatMessageReceivedInThread` (and sibling) event enqueues exactly one job onto the EXISTING `Services/Jobs/` Service Bus contract (no new queue/pipeline), carrying the ACS message id + thread id 031 needs.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An unvalidated / wrong-topic delivery does NOT enqueue a job; a malformed payload returns ProblemDetails and enqueues nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The endpoint is thin — it does NOT persist `sprk_communication`, normalize the event, run enrichment, dedupe, or DLQ inline (those are 031).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No client-side ACS SDK is introduced; any Event Grid/ACS client uses the central `TokenCredential` (no `new` credential).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">If feature-gated, the endpoint is registered unconditionally with an ADR-032 Null-Object service.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; existing inbound/job tests pass; publish-size delta reported vs ~45.30 MB (≤60 MB); no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends on 012 (per-customer ACS resource + Event Grid system topic/subscription + dead-letter Storage — the endpoint is the subscription target) and 021 (the `ICommunicationChannelIngestor` seam the eventual job handler calls). Blocks 031 (the Service Bus job handler that normalizes + persists idempotently + DLQs). `parallel-safe: true` within W3, but 031 is serial after 030 (031 consumes this task's job envelope contract).

    Strict scope: validated webhook ingress + handshake + enqueue. Idempotency/echo-dedup, the ACS-event→`NormalizedMessage` normalizer, the persist via `MessagingIngestor`, and the DLQ are ALL 031. Keep the endpoint fast + thin so Event Grid's at-least-once retries don't stack — durability + dedupe are the queue's + 031's job.
  </notes>

